   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 30739805,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 3322966,
    "poster_id": 571016,
    "post_rendered": "For a right angled triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\"  width=\"58\" height=\"13\" > with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/d/69dc69de622548c19c1bba7643a95ebfec75280c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A=90$\"  width=\"68\" height=\"13\" > we have <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/0/0d05cc474df0742d7c420fb62698079096c330ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=2AB$\"  width=\"88\" height=\"13\" >.</span> Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" > is the midpoint of side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\"  width=\"28\" height=\"12\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" > is incenter of triangle <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\"  width=\"58\" height=\"13\" >.</span> The line passing trough <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" > and perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/b/35bb3f3bcadf5dc5c045b80fc24d014c0b969cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BI$\"  width=\"24\" height=\"12\" > intersect with lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/b/35bb3f3bcadf5dc5c045b80fc24d014c0b969cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BI$\"  width=\"24\" height=\"12\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\"  width=\"27\" height=\"13\" > at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" > respectively. If the semi-line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/6/f8631a9a7518bf0907936d1e96defe9cf7c19cef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IK$\"  width=\"26\" height=\"12\" > cuts circumcircle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\"  width=\"58\" height=\"13\" > at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" > be the second intersection point of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffb105232a8a0e6307866e5d52ccb9e6db45c33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FH$\"  width=\"30\" height=\"12\" > with circumcircle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\"  width=\"58\" height=\"13\" > , then prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/d/64ddf097bfa83d428e59497177c6f71249d98278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" > is tangent to the incircle of triangle <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\"  width=\"58\" height=\"13\" >.</span><br>\n<br>\n<i>Proposed by Mahdi Etesami Fard</i>",
    "post_canonical": "For a right angled triangle $\\triangle ABC$ with $\\angle A=90$ we have $AC=2AB$. Point $M$ is the midpoint of side $BC$ and $I$ is incenter of triangle $\\triangle ABC$. The line passing trough $M$ and perpendicular to $BI$ intersect with lines $BI$ and $AC$ at points $H$ and $K$ respectively. If the semi-line $IK$ cuts circumcircle of triangle $\\triangle ABC$ at $F$ and $S$ be the second intersection point of line $FH$ with circumcircle of triangle $\\triangle ABC$ , then prove that $SM$ is tangent to the incircle of triangle $\\triangle ABC$.\n\n[i]Proposed by Mahdi Etesami Fard[/i]",
