    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 3322976,
    "poster_id": 571016,
    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\"  width=\"58\" height=\"13\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/4/2b4dd002e473d1e9e4bf3d1d51a4803601a7ff9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle C&#039;B&#039;A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"19\" > be two congruent triangles ( with this order and orient. ). Define point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" > as the midpoint of segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\"  width=\"27\" height=\"13\" > and suppose that the extension of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/f/3ff8f9cb3df232f1fece3d69ea5757773ea997ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB&#039;$\"  width=\"32\" height=\"14\" > from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#039;$\"  width=\"18\" height=\"14\" > passes trough <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" > , if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" > be a point on the smaller arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/5/4d5ee546f7ea84755eae7a58fbf1d892bd258118.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MC$\"  width=\"33\" height=\"12\" > of circumcircle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/a/0faed260933ee64e9300b5750492d63184fc7687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BMC$\"  width=\"64\" height=\"13\" > such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7c6c73f9267468ae03fce529e4c953eb70533fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FB&#039;A=90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"104\" height=\"16\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/2/6a20837ad8c01ab68542463a8198a6cbed2c35ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle C&#039;CB&#039; \\neq 90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"19\" > , then prove that <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/9/0c96d64768fed879db073604f32be8130c63a562.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B&#039;C&#039;C=\\angle CAF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"146\" height=\"16\" >.</span><br>\n<br>\n<i>Proposed by Alireza Dadgarnia</i>",
    "post_canonical": "Let $\\triangle ABC$ and $\\triangle C'B'A$ be two congruent triangles ( with this order and orient. ). Define point $M$ as the midpoint of segment $AB$ and suppose that the extension of $CB'$ from $B'$ passes trough $M$ , if $F$ be a point on the smaller arc $MC$ of circumcircle of triangle $\\triangle BMC$ such that $\\angle FB'A=90$ and $\\angle C'CB' \\neq 90$ , then prove that $\\angle B'C'C=\\angle CAF$.\n\n[i]Proposed by Alireza Dadgarnia[/i]",
