    "topic_id": 3322978,
    "poster_id": 571016,
    "post_rendered": "Find all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/0/e10159a7f8461427e19d333863a9a1faf60b5685.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f : \\mathbb{Q}[x] \\to \\mathbb{Q}[x]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"20\" > such that two following conditions holds :<br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/0/910edb3f53a2a2d1f34e1e450fc6ad792cad78db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"$$\\forall P , Q \\in \\mathbb{Q}[x] : f(P+Q)=f(P)+f(Q)$$\"  width=\"315\" height=\"18\" ><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/3/bb3780ae10f2b5439c33b3e0b7efee9ed85cd462.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"$$\\forall P \\in \\mathbb{Q}[x] : gcd(P , f(P))=1 \\iff$$\"  width=\"272\" height=\"18\" ><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" > is square-free.<br>\n<br>\n<br>\nWhich a square-free polynomial with rational coefficients is a polynomial such that there doesn&#039;t exist square of a non-constant polynomial with rational coefficients that divides it.<br>\n<br>\n<i>Proposed by Sina Azizedin</i>",
    "post_canonical": "Find all functions $f : \\mathbb{Q}[x] \\to \\mathbb{Q}[x]$ such that two following conditions holds :\n$$\\forall P , Q \\in \\mathbb{Q}[x] : f(P+Q)=f(P)+f(Q)$$\n$$\\forall P \\in \\mathbb{Q}[x] : gcd(P , f(P))=1 \\iff$$\n$P$ is square-free.\n\n\nWhich a square-free polynomial with rational coefficients is a polynomial such that there doesn't exist square of a non-constant polynomial with rational coefficients that divides it.\n\n[i]Proposed by Sina Azizedin[/i]",
