    "post_rendered": "Prove that for any natural numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/6/bd61c9b7f2398dddffbb65aa94614b43a660a7e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a , b , c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" > that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/7/fd78bcb8d40ee2dc69cf5e7ca921a4e80b7b3b3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;a&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/c/7ac2a5b1d71ed206ed30dd86732360e76b3b59d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$gcd(c,ab)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"109\" height=\"20\" > , there exist a natural number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" > such that :<br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22e443ce07bded3e49255cb9c31c5825b5780046.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"$$c | \\binom{b^n}{a^n}$$\"  width=\"55\" height=\"53\" ><br>\n<i>Proposed by Navid Safaei</i>",
    "post_canonical": "Prove that for any natural numbers $a , b , c$ that $b>a>1$ and $gcd(c,ab)=1$ , there exist a natural number $n$ such that :\n$$c | \\binom{b^n}{a^n}$$\n\n[i]Proposed by Navid Safaei[/i]",
