    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 3322988,
    "poster_id": 571016,
    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/b/74b8509880feedf248af3be52483dd593c83fad7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&lt;k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" > be two natural numbers and suppose that Sepehr has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" > chemical elements , <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8ea7ee8a282949fd853a01537ec7a2b55e56f75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k$\"  width=\"18\" height=\"12\" > grams from each , divided arbitrarily in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8ea7ee8a282949fd853a01537ec7a2b55e56f75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k$\"  width=\"18\" height=\"12\" > cups.Find the smallest number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" > such that there is always possible for Sepehr to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" > cups , containing at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" > grams from each element in total.<br>\n<br>\n<i>Proposed by Josef Tkadlec &amp; Morteza Saghafian</i>",
    "post_canonical": "Let $n<k$ be two natural numbers and suppose that Sepehr has $n$ chemical elements , $2k$ grams from each , divided arbitrarily in $2k$ cups.Find the smallest number $b$ such that there is always possible for Sepehr to choose $b$ cups , containing at least $2$ grams from each element in total.\n\n[i]Proposed by Josef Tkadlec & Morteza Saghafian[/i]",
